  Apr 24 02:51:35 ... GSSAPI client step 2

Timeline mapping:
- 02:51:35 — sssd restart (GSSAPI/Kerberos auth to FreeIPA)
- 02:52:32 — kustomize-controller first failure (connection refused)
- 02:52:39 — pods start restarting cascade
- 02:52:52 — calico-kube-controllers exit 255 (killed by liveness)
- 02:53:00 — host PSI peaks 54%
- 02:53:07 — more pods terminating

57-second window sssd restart → cascade.

THEORY:
- SSSD is FreeIPA/LDAP client
- During reconnect, NSS lookups block (up to 6s timeout)
- PAM operations block
- Kubelet exec probes inside containers hang on NSS
- Probes time out → pods marked unhealthy → restart cascade

Supporting evidence:
- calico-node probe: exec [/bin/calico-node -felix-live -bird-live] timeout=10s
- This is EXEC probe — spawns process inside container
- Process spawn does NSS lookups
- If sssd stuck, exec hangs 10s → probe fails

Proposed fix:
  # nsswitch.conf — files first
  passwd: files sss systemd
  group:  files sss systemd

  # sssd.conf caching
  [domain/...]
  cache_credentials = True
  entry_cache_timeout = 600
  offline_credentials_expiration = 2

  # Probe timeout increases
  kubectl patch daemonset calico-node --type json -p='[
    {"op": "replace", "path": "/spec/template/spec/containers/0/livenessProbe/timeoutSeconds", "value": 30},
    {"op": "replace", "path": "/spec/template/spec/containers/0/livenessProbe/failureThreshold", "value": 10}
  ]'

